  "description": "The \u0027dss_codeenvs_cached\u0027 dataset provides a comprehensive overview of various code environments used within a system, capturing essential details about each environment. This dataset is particularly useful for managing and auditing code environments, as it includes information on the environment\u0027s name, programming language, deployment mode, and owner. Additionally, it provides technical details such as the Python interpreter version and core packages set, which are crucial for ensuring compatibility and performance. The dataset also includes the file path and URL for accessing each environment, facilitating easy navigation and management. This dataset is valuable for system administrators, developers, and data scientists who need to maintain and optimize code environments, ensuring they are up-to-date and properly configured. It can also aid in troubleshooting and auditing by providing a clear record of the environments in use, their configurations, and responsible parties.",
  "shortDesc": "Dataset of cached code environments with details on language, deployment, and access.",
